{"kind":"request","text":"planner: durable writers outside the resolver's default. claude scoped this out of the resident-default review and it predates that head: gs actor-add, actor-retire, role-grant and role-revoke have no --server flag, so they always write locally while every other durable writer now defaults to the repository's advertised resident; cmd/gitseq-github takes an explicit --server with no default. With the configuration boundary no longer serialising across processes, a local write racing the resident is exactly the lost-update class assert ffa76a57 recorded and which struck twice more tonight. Proposal: give the four commands the same resolveServerURL default (or an explicit decision that they are single-writer tools) and give cmd/gitseq-github a default.","body":{"conditions":"Decide whether the four authority commands join the advertised-resident default or are documented single-writer tools, and whether cmd/gitseq-github gains a default. If work is wanted, file it to an implementer with conditions; otherwise record the decision so the gap stops being invisible.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}